            <ArticleTitle>[Abdominal tumor after persistent coughing and uncontrolled anticoagulation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157/a000007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 83-year-old female patient with ST elevation myocardial infarction who developed a rectus sheath hematoma during treatment with antiplatelet medication and systemic anticoagulants following cough attacks. The patient presented with progressive pain in the left lower abdomen associated with a palpable mass and anaemia. Abdominal sonography and computed tomography revealed a rectus sheath hematoma. We discuss pathogenesis, clinical findings, diagnostic workup and therapy. Moreover, we review the current related literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
